--- title Collecting values as code runs
--- about COLLECT and KEEP as ordinary functions, which is a different
--- about thing from the PARSE keywords of the same names. COLLECT
--- about evaluates a block and answers what KEEP put aside while it
--- about ran, so the gathering is not tied to matching at all. Rebol's
--- about own SPLIT is built on them.

--- id collecting/keeping-two-values
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold collect [keep 1 keep 2]
--- result
"[1 2]"

--- id collecting/collecting-nothing
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold collect []
--- result
"[]"

--- id collecting/a-block-is-spread-by-default
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note Which is the surprise, and the reason /only exists.
--- code
mold collect [keep [1 2]]
--- result
"[1 2]"

--- id collecting/keeping-a-block-whole
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- code
mold collect [keep/only [1 2]]
--- result
"[[1 2]]"

--- id collecting/keeping-from-inside-a-loop
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- note The point of having it as a function rather than a parse rule:
--- note anything that runs can keep, including a loop.
--- code
mold collect [repeat i 3 [keep i]]
--- result
"[1 2 3]"
